From 48aec596a4b0187ed2de04122e5dd7023fe31fc2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 05:01:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(web): center short forms on wide screens, add missing
 Pool card, use design tokens on Pool stats

- Wallet (no-wallet / locked states) and Multisig: vertically center
  the form within available height instead of pinning to the top,
  so short forms don't look unfinished on wide desktop viewports.
  Active-wallet view (with balance/history) is untouched since it
  has enough content to fill the space naturally.
- Home grid: Pool was a fully built, linked-in-nav page but missing
  from the home card grid entirely (7 cards existed, covering every
  other route). Added a Mining pool card and moved to a 4-column
  grid so 8 cards divide evenly (4+4) instead of 7 leaving a lonely
  card in the last row.
- Pool stats: replaced ad-hoc Tailwind colors (indigo-400, sky-400,
  emerald-400, amber-400, green-400) with the app's existing design
  tokens (blue, teal, ok, gold) already used identically on Network,
  Roadmap, and the explorer asset badges. Also removed  types
  on StatCard props in favor of LucideIcon / string | number.

Verified with tsc --noEmit and eslint (no new warnings/errors);
screenshot-checked desktop + mobile before and after.
